A textPath in Ladybird now follows the referenced path mapped through
that path element’s own transform, and not through the transforms of
its ancestors. Blink does the same in LayoutSVGTextPath::LayoutPath(),
which transforms the path data by the element’s CalculateTransform();
WebKit in RenderSVGTextPath::layoutPath(), with the shape renderer’s
computeRendererTransform(); and Gecko in SVGTextFrame::GetTextPath(),
with the geometry element’s LocalTransform(). In Chrome 158 and
Firefox 151, the reftest and its reference render identically. And in
Chrome 158, Firefox 151, and WebKit 26.5, text on a translated path
gets the bounding box of text on the same path with the translation
baked into its coordinates.
